      "nets": ["FLOAT_HIGH", "FLOAT_LOW", "+3V3", "GND"],
      "observed": "In the 'Safety Switches' block the +3V3 10 k resistor R6 is drawn on the upper row together with the FLOAT_HIGH net, and the GND 10 k resistor R9 is drawn on the lower row together with the FLOAT_LOW net (R6 pulls FLOAT_HIGH up, R9 pulls FLOAT_LOW down).",
      "expected": "Spec section 4.4 states the reference wiring is 'R6 FLOAT_LOW +3V3 10k, R9 GND FLOAT_HIGH 10k', i.e. R6 must pull FLOAT_LOW up to +3V3 and R9 must pull FLOAT_HIGH down to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R6 FLOAT_LOW +3V3 10k, R9 GND FLOAT_HIGH 10k"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Safety Switches: R6 10k / C5 100n on the FLOAT_HIGH row; R9 10k / C4 100n on the FLOAT_LOW row"}
      ],
      "impact": "The idle level of both float interlocks is inverted. FLOAT_HIGH idles high, so the high-level overflow interlock (R11/T4/T5) keeps the ATO valve switch permanently off; FLOAT_LOW idles low, so the low-level pump cutoff (R2/T1/T2) no longer disables the main pump as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.45
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["H6"],
      "pins": ["H6.1", "H6.2", "H6.3", "H6.4"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "I2C_SDA", "I2C_SCL", "GND"],
      "observed": "The optional environmental-sensor header H6 is wired pin1=+5V, pin2=I2C_SDA, pin3=I2C_SCL, pin4=GND, while the otherwise identical light-sensor header H5 is wired pin1=+3V3, pin2=I2C_SCL, pin3=I2C_SDA, pin4=GND.",
      "expected": "Spec section 4.1: 'H5, H6 (4-pin JST-PH headers) - each breaks out +3V3, GND, I2C_SCL, I2C_SDA' - H6 should therefore be powered from +3V3 and carry SCL/SDA in the same order as H5.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "H5, H6 (4-pin JST-PH headers) - each breaks out +3V3, GND, I2C_SCL, I2C_SDA"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Environmental Sensor (optional): H6 JST_PH pin1 +5V, pin2 I2C_SDA, pin3 I2C_SCL, pin4 GND"}
      ],
      "impact": "A plug-in BME280 wired for the H5 pin order would have SDA and SCL reversed (bus non-functional) and would be fed from the 5 V rail instead of 3.3 V.",
      "confidence": 0.35
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing largely matches the specification, but two connection-level deviations were found: the float-switch pull resistors R6/R9 appear to be placed on the opposite float nets from the specified R6->FLOAT_LOW(+3V3)/R9->FLOAT_HIGH(GND) arrangement, inverting the ATO/overflow and low-level pump interlocks, and the environmental-sensor header H6 is powered from +5V with SDA/SCL swapped relative to the equivalent H5 header, contrary to the spec's '+3V3, GND, I2C_SCL, I2C_SDA' statement."
}

